From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Input: s6sy761 - add an optional reset gpio

s6sy761_power_on() confirms the controller came back by reading one event
and requiring it to be S6SY761_INFO_BOOT_COMPLETE. That only happens if
the controller actually restarted, and the driver assumes dropping vdd and
avdd is enough to guarantee it.

On a board that shares one of those supplies the assumption fails. On the
OnePlus 7T Pro, avdd is the same rail that feeds the WCN3990 Wi-Fi chip, so
whenever Wi-Fi is up the regulator stays enabled, the controller never
restarts, no boot-complete event is produced, and system resume fails with
-ENODEV.

Take an optional reset line and pulse it around the supply change so the
restart happens regardless of who else holds the rails. Boards that do not
describe the line keep the previous behaviour exactly.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/unaligned.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/input/mt.h>
 #include <linux/input/touchscreen.h>
@@ -101,6 +102,7 @@
 struct s6sy761_data {
 	struct i2c_client *client;
 	struct regulator_bulk_data regulators[2];
+	struct gpio_desc *reset_gpio;
 	struct input_dev *input;
 	struct touchscreen_properties prop;
 
@@ -299,6 +301,19 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The controller only reports a completed boot after it has actually
+	 * restarted. Dropping the supplies is not enough to guarantee that:
+	 * a board may share one of them with another consumer that keeps it
+	 * up. Pulse reset when the board describes the line, so the restart
+	 * happens regardless of who else holds the rails.
+	 */
+	if (sdata->reset_gpio) {
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sdata->reset_gpio, 1);
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sdata->reset_gpio, 0);
+	}
+
 	msleep(140);
 
 	/* double check whether the touch is functional */
@@ -382,6 +397,8 @@
 	struct s6sy761_data *sdata = data;
 
 	disable_irq(sdata->client->irq);
+	if (sdata->reset_gpio)
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sdata->reset_gpio, 1);
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(sdata->regulators),
 						sdata->regulators);
 }
@@ -412,6 +429,12 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	sdata->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(&client->dev, "reset",
+						    GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	if (IS_ERR(sdata->reset_gpio))
+		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, PTR_ERR(sdata->reset_gpio),
+				     "failed to get reset gpio\n");
+
 	err = devm_add_action_or_reset(&client->dev, s6sy761_power_off, sdata);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
--
2.50.1
